## Claim
Text: "U.S. President Donald Trump has departed Walter Reed hospital just a few days after testing positive for COVID-19."
Claim date: October 05, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Was Donald Trump serving as the President of the United States in October 2020?
Answer: Yes, Donald Trump was serving as the President of the United States in October 2020, as evidenced by the September 16, 2020, article referring to him as "President Donald Trump" during a White House press briefing.

Source URL: https://www.cnbc.com/2020/09/16/trump-says-he-thinks-us-could-start-distributing-a-coronavirus-vaccine-in-october.html

### Did Donald Trump receive a positive test result for COVID-19 in late September or early October 2020?
Answer: Yes. According to the BBC source, "Mr Trump tweeted early on Friday morning that he and First Lady Melania Trump had both tested positive" for COVID-19, which corresponds to October 2, 2020 — right in line with early October 2020 and just days before the claim date of October 5, 2020.

Source URL: https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/av/world-us-canada-54395564

### On what specific date did Donald Trump's positive COVID-19 test result become publicly confirmed?
Answer: Donald Trump's positive COVID-19 test result became publicly confirmed on **October 2, 2020**. As the article states, "Trump tweeted just before 1 a.m." that day, writing, "Tonight, @FLOTUS and I tested positive for COVID-19. We will begin our quarantine and recovery process immediately."

Source URL: https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/president-trump-and-first-lady-test-positive-for-covid-19

### Was Donald Trump admitted to Walter Reed National Military Medical Center in connection with his COVID-19 diagnosis?
Answer: Yes, according to the source, Donald Trump was admitted to Walter Reed National Military Medical Center in connection with his COVID-19 diagnosis. The article states that "President Donald Trump was hospitalized at Walter Reed National Military Medical Center in Maryland after testing positive for COVID-19," with the White House announcing the plan on Friday afternoon as a precautionary measure, at the recommendation of his physician and medical experts.

Source URL: https://www.teenvogue.com/story/trump-has-covid-19-melania-hope-hicks-tested-positive

### On what specific date was Donald Trump admitted to Walter Reed National Military Medical Center?
Answer: Donald Trump was admitted to Walter Reed National Military Medical Center on Friday, October 2, 2020, arriving at 6:29 p.m.

Source URL: https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2020-10-02/pence-tests-negative-as-white-house-scrambles-to-deal-with-its-coronavirus-outbreak

### Did Donald Trump depart from Walter Reed National Military Medical Center on or around October 5, 2020?
Answer: Yes, the search result confirms that Donald Trump departed from Walter Reed National Military Medical Center on Monday, October 5, 2020. Trump himself tweeted, "I will be leaving the great Walter Reed Medical Center today at 6:30 P.M." The article notes he had spent three nights at the hospital being treated for COVID-19 before returning to the White House via Marine One.

Source URL: https://www.cbsnews.com/baltimore/news/president-trump-coronavirus-condition-walter-reed-latest/

### On what specific date and time did Donald Trump leave Walter Reed National Military Medical Center?
Answer: Donald Trump left Walter Reed National Military Medical Center on Monday, October 5, 2020, at 6:30 P.M. As he tweeted that day, "I will be leaving the great Walter Reed Medical Center today at 6:30 P.M." He traveled back to the White House aboard the presidential helicopter, Marine One.

Source URL: https://www.cbsnews.com/baltimore/news/president-trump-coronavirus-condition-walter-reed-latest/

### How many days elapsed between Donald Trump's confirmed positive COVID-19 test and his departure from Walter Reed National Military Medical Center?
Answer: Donald Trump's positive COVID-19 test result was announced on Friday, October 2, 2020, and he departed Walter Reed hospital on Monday, October 5, meaning three days elapsed. As reported, he was "hospitalised for three days."

Source URL: https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/av/world-us-canada-54395564

### Was Donald Trump officially discharged by medical professionals or did he leave Walter Reed under other circumstances (such as against medical advice)?
Answer: Donald Trump was officially discharged by medical professionals after meeting hospital discharge criteria. His physician Sean Conley stated that "he’s met or exceeded all standard hospital discharge criteria" and would continue to be monitored at home, indicating a medically sanctioned release.

Source URL: https://www.vox.com/2020/10/5/21502048/trump-discharged-walter-reed-medical-center-hospital-covid-coronavirus

### Did reputable news organizations or official White House communications report on October 5, 2020, that Donald Trump had departed Walter Reed hospital?
Answer: Yes, reputable news organizations reported on October 5, 2020, that Donald Trump would depart Walter Reed hospital that day. The CBS News article states, "I will be leaving the great Walter Reed Medical Center today at 6:30 P.M.," Trump tweeted. "Feeling really good! Don't be afraid of Covid. ... I feel better than I did 20 years ago!"

Source URL: https://www.cbsnews.com/baltimore/news/president-trump-coronavirus-condition-walter-reed-latest/

## Final Judgement
Based on the recorded evidence, the fact-check establishes all necessary facts with clarity. Donald Trump was the sitting President in October 2020. He publicly confirmed his positive COVID-19 test on October 2, 2020, was admitted to Walter Reed hospital that same evening, and officially departed from the hospital on the afternoon of October 5, 2020, after being medically discharged. This timeline confirms that his departure occurred "just a few days" after testing positive.

The evidence is definitive, requiring no further investigation.

Therefore, the facts gathered directly support and confirm the claim. `supported`

### Verdict: SUPPORTED

